# F0 operational gate proposal — 2026-11-01

**F0 remains open.** The architectural authority adopts “foundation and contracts” and a dependency on risk/platform decisions. It does not adopt an operational closure specification. This document makes all seven predecessor rows verifiable without making them adopted requirements. The predecessor is preserved in docs/validation/f0-reconciliation-20261101/before/docs/validation/foundation-current-20261101/f0.md.bin.

The maintainer is the decision owner. Proposed boundary for decision: Linux x86_64 foundation/contracts, the existing bounded local host/runtime/verifier/UI slices, criterion-bound evidence and preservation. Defer durable history to a separately authorized next slice and before MVP; defer public plugins/agents, remote access, production sandbox claims, other OS targets and public distribution. This is a recommendation, not an adopted exclusion or a claim that present code is sufficient. POL-02 says local persistence **at MVP**, not at F0; only a new explicit milestone decision can include it in F0. Including it leaves F0-P04 blocked until actual storage acceptance.

The complete machine-readable matrix is [f0-matrix.json](../f0-reconciliation-20261101/f0-matrix.json). Each entry records requirement/origin, adoption, scope, objective pass condition, oracle, inputs, evidence, five-state verdict, limitations and exact remaining action. “PROPOSED” describes authority, not a sixth acceptance state.

| ID / authority | Objective pass condition and method | Available evidence / limit | State | Remaining action |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| F0-P01 / POL-01, bootstrap ADR, architecture F0 | Named platform; check/fmt/clippy/tests, explicit X11 and Wayland render/interaction/exit; inspect first-party unsafe prohibition | Bootstrap and local-task-ui evidence envelopes; scoped display observations, no new run | INCONCLUSIVE | Maintainer adopts envelope; executor maps assertions and environment to the gate |
| F0-P02 / architecture F0, POL-04/05/10 | Adopted disposition for each applicable OPEN-01..11 risk; test any claimed controls against denied effects | Existing local decisions; complete risk acceptance absent | UNVERIFIED | Maintainer adopts decision docket, with exclusions and revisit triggers |
