## Current diagnosis and minimal boundary

The immediate sequencing blocker is adoption of the F0 boundary, but closure is
also blocked by incomplete evidence coverage. It is not established that approval
alone would finish F0, nor that new foundation code is necessary. The source
inspection establishes one concrete missing implementation: durable history. Under
the proposed boundary it belongs to the separate pre-MVP delivery, not F0.

Read-only comparison in `../f0-reconciliation-20261101/decision-preparation/product-bindings.json`
found no mismatches in 3,514 declared input/artifact bindings across 38 observations
of bootstrap, host, runtime, verifier and local-task-ui. This establishes byte
agreement only. It does not authenticate historical runs, reobserve today's display
environment, discover undeclared dependencies or approve the seven F0 rows.
The earlier reference to check/fmt/clippy/test logs under foundation-current was
not resolvable; use raw artifact paths in the individual feature envelopes.

For F0-P03, inspect host tests `real_process_negotiation_shutdown_and_recovery`,
`incompatible_and_unauthorized_are_rejected`,
`malformed_oversized_and_wrong_correlation_fail_closed` and
`timeout_and_crash_are_distinct_and_bounded`. For F0-P05, inspect verifier cases
`approval_requires_observation_not_completion_claims`,
`failure_history_survives_repair_and_content_invalidation_is_selective`,
`incomplete_and_not_applicable_are_not_approval` and
`contradictory_current_pass_does_not_erase_observed_failure`, together with UI
`real_result_identity_history_invalidation_and_preservation` and the graphical
acceptance review. These are existing candidate oracles, not new execution results.

Proposed minimum: existing Rust/Iced foundation; bounded trusted local host/runtime
contracts; controlled task UI; independent verification, preservation and current
input semantics. No requirement to integrate the host into the UI, support a real
agent, implement full engines or deliver persistent history just to close F0.
This proposal retains all original obligations for explicit disposition; it does
not waive a currently applicable policy or silently shrink an adopted criterion.

## Decision form and smallest remaining work

No answer is recorded. The maintainer may adopt or amend each item:

| Decision | Proposed answer | Consequence / revisit |
|---|---|---|
| F0-D1 | Adopt F0-P01..03/05/06 within the current Linux x86_64 local fixture envelope and the risk docket below | Preserve distinct X11/Wayland limitations; revisit any platform, permissions or public contract change |
| F0-D2 | Defer F0-P04 to product-local-persistence, accepted after F0 and before F3/MVP | Session history remains volatile until that delivery; restart artifacts must not be advertised as restored acceptance |
| F0-D3 | Defer full engines, real agents, public SDK/distribution and platform expansion in F0-P07 to their roadmap features | F1..F8 remain open; local extensibility and preservation duties still apply |
| F0-D4 | Explicitly interpret/extend legacy succession only for obsolete skill-status clauses listed in legacy-succession.md | Preserve lineage, recovery and applicable package/rights obligations; no blanket waiver or transfer of 36 skill approvals |

Compatibility: POL-02 requires local persistence at MVP; the architecture names F0
as foundation/contracts and F3 as MVP, without assigning storage to F0. Therefore
the proposed independent delivery between F0 and MVP is compatible with those
texts. It does not prove MVP readiness or complete F1/F2/F3. The maintainer must
adopt the milestone assignment; the constitution and roadmap remain unchanged.

| Work / owner | Dependency | Observable completion |
|---|---|---|
| G1 / maintainer | This proposal | Recorded F0-D1..D4 and OPEN dispositions; each inclusion/deferral has rationale and trigger |
| G2 / executor | G1 | Per-clause mapping for P01/03/05/06 to actual assertions, raw artifacts and bound inputs; explicit missing evidence and contradictions |
| G3 / executor | G2; effective test permissions | Only missing or affected observations collected; no skip counted as pass. New defects receive bounded fixes only within authorized scope |
| G4 / executor + maintainer | G3 | Every applicable gate APPROVED or justified NOT APPLICABLE; explicit F0 closure record |
| P1 / maintainer, then executor | Separate experiment grant and adopted corpus/bounds | Paired snapshots/SQLite results and dependency review; no product integration |
| P2 / maintainer, then executor | G4, P1 results, technology decision and integration grant | Independently accepted product-local-persistence before MVP |

G1 is the next decision; G2 is the next executable verification work after it.
Planning does not require new product code. P1 scheduling may be authorized
separately, but persistence delivery remains after F0 under this proposal.

## Risk and platform decision docket

| Open decision | Already adopted/observed | F0 decision still needed | Proposed disposition and revisit trigger |
|---|---|---|---|
| OPEN-01 | Linux x86_64; scoped X11/Xwayland and human Wayland observations | Name OS/display/filesystem support and residual GNOME input limit | Confine initial envelope to identified local environment; reevaluate on OS/FS/GPU/display change |
| OPEN-02 | Rust 1.99.1, edition 2024, declared floor 1.99, Iced 0.14.0 | Confirm this F0 matrix; no demonstrated 1.99.0 minimum | Retain pinned toolchain, std local supervision and Iced thread-pool; revisit external I/O |
| OPEN-03 | ASCII 1.0/Unix socket fixture only | Contract stability, version/failure boundary sufficient for F0? | Bounded fixture contract; public JSON-RPC/ACP/SDK deferred until adapters |
| OPEN-04 | Controlled local task, no real agents/network/credentials | Accept permitted effects and direct-child limits for F0 | No autonomous replay/remote providers; revisit adapters and grants |
| OPEN-05 | Local MVP policy, in-memory history today | Include persistence in F0 or explicitly defer? | Separate next feature; location, retention, durability and engine require decision |
| OPEN-06 | No product sandbox, effective environment permissions | Accept trusted local-fixture risk, or require actual isolation in F0? | No sandbox claim; inclusion requires threat model and denied-effect OS tests |
| OPEN-07 | Own GPL decision; third-party rights unresolved | Is any distribution/public SDK included in F0? | Defer publication; retain rights blocker and separate artifact qualification obligations |
| OPEN-08 | No product CPU/RAM/latency/accessibility target adopted | Which responsiveness/accessibility obligations are F0 gates? | Keep existing graphical assertions; additional targets require named corpus/hardware and authorization |
| OPEN-09 | First-party forbid unsafe; native/transitive dependencies exist | Accept reviewed dependency/FFI risk or add a dependency audit gate? | No blanket absence-of-C claim; revisit new storage/driver/parser |
| OPEN-10 | Future hypotheses only | Confirm outside F0 | Revisit only with explicit feature authorization |
| OPEN-11 | Controlled existing UI; final UX/language choices open | Define required approval/error/stale presentation for F0 | Retain explicit verification and visible failure; broader UX remains separately scoped |

These decisions cannot be delegated to a successful test or a checkbox. A maintainer decision must identify alternatives, consequences, exclusions and review triggers. No owner acceptance is recorded here.

## Execution and closure procedure

1. Maintainer records adopted boundary and dispositions by F0-P ID, including F0-P04 and unresolved legacy succession scope. Preserve this proposal and original clauses.
2. Executor stabilizes adopted criteria and maps exact implementation/oracle/configuration/environment inputs; use the full traceability and five-state contract in sdd/evidence.md. A statement of scope is not operational evidence.
3. Compare retained bindings before selecting reruns. Existing code/oracles were not changed in this documentary task, so Cargo/GUI consumer runs are not repeated solely for document updates. The inherited 25-criterion review is not independently audited or rerun here. Targeted structural/freshness/mutation checks and documentary comparisons are recorded in ../f0-reconciliation-20261101/checks.json.
4. For changed functional inputs, confirm commands in README and prerequisites: Rust 1.99.1 and cached dependencies, local socket permission, actual named X11/Wayland environment, graphical input permission/human observer. Run check/fmt/clippy/tests and explicit ignored desktop cases only where affected. A skipped graphical case is not approval. Persistence has no implemented oracle yet; follow its proposed feature after authorization.
5. Collect per-criterion failures, negative controls, logs, versions and limitations. ZIP qualification, rights, production controls and unavailable observations remain dependencies, never structural substitutes.
6. Close F0 only after scope adoption and every applicable gate is APPROVED or explicitly justified NOT APPLICABLE under that scope. Any REJECTED, INCONCLUSIVE or UNVERIFIED applicable row prevents closure. Do not sum the 25 legacy states or the 36 skill verdicts into F0 acceptance.
